[2026-09-17 19:21:24] REQ 260917144049-462 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=934 roles=assistant,user,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":"0076 closed -- pin ratified, scope stays test-files-only, revisit trigger noted.\n\n---\n\n**Next: 0079 -- camera .103 video-track death.** This one's fresh and current (filed 19:00Z, ~15 min ago).\n\nFacts: ext3 (.103) video track died on the producer connection ~18:05Z; audio still flows. go2rtc can't re-establish the video session (read i/o timeout on every dial) → restream 404s → frigate ffmpeg 404-loops. **No ext3 recordings since 18:05Z.** I verified live: hour-19 dir has zero ext3 segments while all other cameras are recording normally. Camera is up (HTTP 200, RTSP control answers) but degraded (ping 344ms vs 22ms for .101; a malformed RTP header warning at 14:52Z -- that's my falsifier probe's minute, likely related).\n\nThe filing asks: **physical power cycle on your next visit** (rides the same visit as .104 power-dead, 0063).\n\nOne thing the filing's cycle agent didn't know: a **remote reboot via thingino HTTP API is possible** but was deliberately not attempted without a ruling (observation-only mode per your 09-16 ruling). Also relevant: my falsifier probe at 17:52Z wedged ext3's recorder and I healed it via stream reload at 17:56Z -- recordings resumed -- but the death at 18:05Z came *after* that heal, so either the reload-heal was incomplete or the camera degraded further. The malformed RTP warning suggests the camera side is sick, not just the session.\n\n**Your call:** (a) physical power cycle on next visit (rides 0063), or (b) authorize the remote reboot now -- one API call, the same thing a power cycle does to the camera's state, and the falsifier's aftermath suggests the camera needs it."},{"role":"user","content":"I'm just going to throw it in here that we are wasting time on the cameras, they are really not that important and they fail so often as to be consuming time and resources for development. I'm lifting the observation-only mode, I thought I already had when I gave you ssh access to them, but I want it stated clearly now, feel free to do anything with or inside them without the need for permission. Again, cameras are just a nice-to-have, not critical at all.\nSo b) it is."},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_rerrzqai","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"# b) authorized: remote reboot of .103. First record the standing ruling, then execute.\n# The thingino reboot API: from the earlier filings, cameras run thingino firmware with HTTP API on port 80. Reboot endpoint is typically /api/reboot or via the web UI. Check the camera's API surface:\nssh -o BatchMode=yes root@10.66.0.5 'curl -s -m 5 -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" http://thingino:thingino@192.168.2.103/metrics 2>/dev/null; echo; curl -s -m 5 -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"http://thingino:thingino@192.168.2.103/\" 2>/dev/null'"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[19:21:21] 200\n200"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_h1t7cgr5","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"# Camera reachable. Thingino reboot: check the known endpoint from prior cycle work (c350 rebooted .105 via cron reboot -f; the HTTP API path). Look in my knowledge for the thingino API recipe:\ngrep -rn \"reboot\" /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/*.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"thingino\\|camera\\|api\\|http\" | head -5"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[19:21:24] /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/audio-death-law-2026-09-12.md:6:process (re)connects while the camera is down (reboot window). The\n/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/audio-death-law-2026-09-12.md:30:int2 connected 30s into its camera's reboot window (connect-during-\n/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/audio-death-law-2026-09-12.md:96:  reboot; the producer renegotiates with the rebooted camera; the\n/root